=============================================================================
SCOPE NOTES (non-binding clarification of the license boundary)
=============================================================================

1. SOURCE CODE — MIT (above). Applies to all original .py source files in this
   repository, including the two independent solver implementations, the
   instance generator, feature extractors, affine-map fitters, scorers,
   analysis/plotting scripts, independent verifiers and tests.

2. DATA AND OUTPUTS — CC-BY-4.0 (Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International,
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Applies to the study-generated
   data and result artifacts: synthetic instance manifests, frozen model
   bundles, lock manifests, raw branch archives (core repo and GitHub Release /
   Zenodo tarballs), result CSV/JSON tables, audits, verification receipts and
   generated figures. Attribution: cite the manuscript (see README.md citation
   placeholder) and this repository/DOI.

3. THIRD-PARTY BENCHMARK TEXTS — NOT covered by the MIT/CC-BY grants above.
   The small benchmark snapshot files are redistributed solely for research
   reproducibility, with original provenance and SHA256 fingerprints recorded
   in experiments/ext_standard_jssp/benchmarks/provenance.json and
   outputs/manifest_lock.json:
     - jobshop1.txt (Lawrence la01–la40 and other classical instances):
       OR-Library, J. E. Beasley (1990), http://people.brunel.ac.uk/~mastjjb/jeb/info.html
     - projects/experiments/benchmark_jobshop.txt, fp_v2_jobshop.txt:
       local frozen archives of classical benchmark texts (OR-Library / Taillard).
     - ta01–ta30: É. Taillard's JSSP instances, obtained from the public JSPLIB
       mirror https://github.com/tamy0612/JSPLIB (instances/ directory).
     - la21–la40 snapshots: parsed from the local jobshop1.txt (OR-Library).
   Original authors retain all rights to these benchmark texts. If your use
   case requires it, obtain the instances directly from the original sources;
   scripts/…/prepare_benchmarks.py re-downloads and fingerprint-verifies the
   Taillard mirror copies. See README.md §Attribution for full citations.
